/**<p>Controls how cache health metrics will be emitted to CloudWatch. Cache health metrics include:</p> <ul> <li> <p>NetworkBandwidthOutAllowanceExceeded: The network packets dropped because the throughput exceeded the aggregated bandwidth limit. This is useful for diagnosing bottlenecks in a cache configuration.</p> </li> <li> <p>EngineCPUUtilization: The CPU utilization (percentage) allocated to the Redis process. This is useful for diagnosing bottlenecks in a cache configuration.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Metrics will be recorded by API ID. You can set the value to <code>ENABLED</code> or <code>DISABLED</code>.</p>
@param healthMetricsConfig Controls how cache health metrics will be emitted to CloudWatch. Cache health metrics include:</p> <ul> <li> <p>NetworkBandwidthOutAllowanceExceeded: The network packets dropped because the throughput exceeded the aggregated bandwidth limit. This is useful for diagnosing bottlenecks in a cache configuration.</p> </li> <li> <p>EngineCPUUtilization: The CPU utilization (percentage) allocated to the Redis process. This is useful for diagnosing bottlenecks in a cache configuration.</p> </li> </ul> <p>Metrics will be recorded by API ID. You can set the value to <code>ENABLED</code> or <code>DISABLED</code>.
@return Returns a reference to this object so that method calls can be chained together.
@see CacheHealthMetricsConfig*/

